{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we start by recalling some properties of angle bisectors in a triangle. The angle bisectors of a triangle intersect at the incenter, which is the center of the inscribed circle. Let's denote the incenter of triangle \\(ABC\\) as \\(I\\). The given condition is that \\(\\angle EDF = 90^\\circ\\), where \\(D\\), \\(E\\), and \\(F\\) are the points where the angle bisectors \\(AD\\), \\(BE\\), and \\(CF\\) intersect the opposite sides of the triangle.\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the measure of the angle formed by two angle bisectors of a triangle is related to the third angle of the triangle. Specifically, if we consider the angle bisectors \\(BE\\) and \\(CF\\) intersecting at \\(I\\), then \\(\\angle EID = 90^\\circ + \\frac{1}{2} \\angle BAC\\). Similarly, if we consider the angle bisectors \\(AD\\) and \\(CF\\) intersecting at \\(I\\), then \\(\\angle DIF = 90^\\circ + \\frac{1}{2} \\angle ABC\\). And if we consider the angle bisectors \\(AD\\) and \\(BE\\) intersecting at \\(I\\), then \\(\\angle AIE = 90^\\circ + \\frac{1}{2} \\angle ACB\\).\n\n","prefix_end":1029,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1191,553,88646,1045,5888,315,9210,14840,10605,304,264,21495,13,576,9210,14840,10605,315,264,21495,31796,518,279,304,3057,11,892,374,279,4126,315,279,1640,17433,12671,13,6771,594,78064,279,304,3057,315,21495,17767,25411,57758,438,17767,40,59,568,576,2661,2971,374,429,1124,11520,4044,468,5262,284,220,24,15,24884,43298,59,701,1380,17767,35,59,701,17767,36,59,701,323,17767,37,57758,525,279,3501,1380,279,9210,14840,10605,17767,1808,59,701,17767,11594,59,701,323,17767,9650,57758,31796,279,14002,11067,315,279,21495,382,5338,11,582,990,279,2097,429,279,6629,315,279,9210,14122,553,1378,9210,14840,10605,315,264,21495,374,5435,311,279,4843,9210,315,279,21495,13,44763,11,421,5